cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite it as below — and please also credit the underlying data,
  the Malaysian Election Corpus (MECo) by Thevesh Thevananthan.
title: "Nadi Demokrasi: Malaysia's Democracy in Numbers"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, citable single-page dashboard that measures seven decades of Malaysian federal
  general elections (1955–2022) with fourteen standard political-science indicators —
  disproportionality, malapportionment, map bias and district compactness (gerrymandering),
  the winner's seat bonus, effective number of parties, multi-cornered contests, volatility,
  seat turnover, marginal seats, turnout, and the descriptive representation of women and ethnic
  communities. Every figure is computed from open data; nothing is hand-entered.
type: software
